  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Resilient Cities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Philippines):  .USAID, through the Climate Resilient Cities (CRC) activity, will advance climate resilience by strengthening the adaptive capacity of select coastal cities to adapt to, and manage climate impacts and disasters. Building on evidence from the Climate Change Capacity Assessment Framework Tool results, USAID will enhance the capacity of Batangas, Legazpi, Iloilo, Borongan, Cotabato, and Zamboanga cities to understand, use, and communicate climate data, including vulnerability and risk data, in urban planning and management. USAID will train cities and improve their capacity to conduct: climate and disaster risk assessments and mainstream results from the analyses in local climate change action plans; land use plans; mapping and geographic information systems; disaster risk reduction operations; emergency operations center management; and basic science communication and messaging. ..USAID will improve the capacity of cities to access and manage climate finance to support local climate adaptation actions. USAID will build capacity to develop and design climate project proposals, improve climate project management, and monitor climate actions and targets. To enable the six cities to implement innovative measures to conserve, restore, and sustainably manage the environment, USAID will complete a menu of nature-based solutions (NBS), producing concept proposals and NBS profiles. USAID will contribute to reducing greenhouse gas emissions by advancing natural climate solutions such as sustainable land management, improved land use planning, and reforestation. USAID will engage with both the national and subnational (city) governments, NGOs, and the private sector to improve the climate resilience and management of urban growth and development in secondary cities. USAID will reduce climate vulnerability and recurrent need for humanitarian assistance and accelerate sustainable development....</narrative>
  </description>
